---
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';

const people = [
  { name: 'Joe Lombard', role: 'Principal' },
  { name: 'Caroline Belz', role: 'Principal' },
  { name: 'Beth Gaudiano', role: 'Account Manager' },
];
---

<Sheet
  title="About Lombard Belz | Precast and AEC Marketing and Association Management"
  description="Lombard Belz is a small marketing and association management firm for the precast and AEC world. The client list stays small on purpose."
  path="/about/"
  sheetName="About"
>
  <!-- OPEN: belief first -->
  <section class="section open">
    <div class="container open__inner">
      <p class="tag">About</p>
      <h1>What we think the work is for.</h1>
      <p class="lede open__identity">
        We think a company should be known to the people who decide what gets
        built before the drawings are done. That belief is the whole practice.
        We do the marketing that makes it true for precast producers and
        suppliers, and we run the associations that hold the industry together,
        from Frankfort, Illinois, for clients across the country.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW THE FIRM IS BUILT -->
  <section class="section story">
    <div class="container story__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="tag reveal">The story</p>
        <h2 class="reveal">Why this firm exists</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          I built Lombard Belz because of two gaps I kept watching from the
          inside. Trade associations were run by one overloaded director, with
          everything in one person's head. Industry marketing was handed to
          outside agencies that learned precast on the client's dime. I had
          lived both, and the fix looked the same from either side: a small
          team that already knows the industry.
        </p>
        <p>
          We still run trade associations in the precast and AEC world today.
          That seat is where the marketing work gets its fluency.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started the firm with my wife, Caroline. She left her career as a
          nurse to build it with me.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2026 we grew beyond the two of us and brought on our first
          employees. When you work with Lombard Belz, the people you meet are
          the people doing the work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PEOPLE -->
  <section class="section people">
    <div class="container people__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="tag reveal">People</p>
        <h2 class="reveal">Who does the work</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="people__list reveal">
        {
          people.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <span class="people__name">{p.name}</span>
              <span class="people__role">{p.role}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE GRANDFATHER RULE -->
  <section class="section creed">
    <div class="container creed__inner">
      <p class="tag reveal">Standing rule</p>
      <blockquote class="creed__quote reveal">
        <p>&ldquo;Pigs get fat, hogs get slaughtered.&rdquo;</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="tag tag--dim reveal">My grandfather's rule</p>
      <p class="dim reveal creed__meaning">
        It is an old saying, but he is the reason it stuck with me. Appetite
        is healthy and greed gets you killed. It still runs this firm. We take
        on work we can do well and turn down the rest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW WE DECIDE -->
  <section class="section decide">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tag reveal">Standing rules</p>
      <h2 class="reveal">How we decide</h2>
      <ul class="decide__list">
        <li class="reveal">
          <p>
            The client list stays small on purpose. We turn down work that
            does not fit, because the right clients matter more than more
            clients.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p>
            We embed in a client's business and treat it like our own. We
            decline engagements where marketing is treated as a box to check.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p>
            Relationships come first. In this industry the people are the
            market, and the model is built on knowing them for decades rather
            than for a campaign.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="reveal">
          <p>
            Client work stays confidential. We publish no names and no case
            studies.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE -->
  <section class="section where">
    <div class="container where__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="tag reveal">Location</p>
        <h2 class="reveal">Based in Frankfort. Working nationwide.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          The firm is based in Frankfort, Illinois, south of Chicago, in the
          corridor where a lot of this country's precast gets made and moved.
          The team works from more than one place, and the client list has
          never been local.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our service area is the United States. Where you are has no bearing
          on whether we fit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="where__link" href="mailto:hello@lombardbelz.com">hello@lombardbelz.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container cta__inner">
      <h2 class="reveal">See if we fit.</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Sheet>

<style>
  .open {
    padding-top: var(--space-section);
  }

  .open__inner {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .open__identity {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .story__grid,
  .people__grid,
  .where__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 6fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .story__grid,
    .people__grid,
    .where__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* People: a plain list, name then role in graphite */
  .people__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .people__list li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.25rem 1.25rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.9rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .people__list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .people__name {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .people__role {
    color: var(--graphite);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  /* The grandfather rule: the page's centerpiece */
  .creed__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .creed__quote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .creed__quote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.6vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .creed__meaning {
    max-width: 32rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .decide__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .decide__list li {
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .decide__list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .decide__list p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .where__link {
    color: var(--black);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .cta__inner {
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
</style>
